{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-A1 report (decision a56c223b). Read-only, at main 356fcd11; no run and no invitation. My promise 6da0ecfc did not take effect (no request), so this report rests on your decision.\n\nThe first step that must fail is followReceipt's entry read, refused by the gateway allow-list before any request leaves the browser.\n\nThe chain, in order:\n1. Enroll posts the join: POST /v1/scopes/\u003cmembership\u003e/acts through the screen transport. The route allows it (application-gateway.ts:55), and the room records the join (items 7 and 10 active).\n2. On \"accepted\", browserRequests calls recorded() (browser-request.ts:91).\n3. recorded() checks the receipt fields locally (browser-joining.ts:~100; no request), then asks for a member session: POST /v1/scopes/\u003cmembership\u003e/sessions (browser-joining.ts:105; client sessions call at :157 of its file). The route allows it (application-gateway.ts:55).\n4. recorded() then calls followReceipt (browser-joining.ts:108). Its first read is this.entry(seq, { at, head: seq }) (handle.ts:236). The HTTP transport adds the read minimum as a query: /v1/scopes/\u003cmembership\u003e/entries/\u003cseq\u003e?atLeast=\u003cencoded\u003e (http.ts:135, via minimumPath).\n5. applicationScreenTransport checks applicationGatewayRoute first (application-gateway.ts, in applicationScreenTransport). The entries rule allows no query: `parts.length === 5 \u0026\u0026 what === \"entries\" … \u0026\u0026 !url.search` (application-gateway.ts:64). So it throws \"This request is outside the application gateway.\"\n6. The HTTP transport turns the throw into a TransportError (http.ts, in call(): \"no reply: …\"), so entry() throws rather than answering unavailable. followReceipt therefore never reaches its fallback read without the minimum (handle.ts:237-241). recorded() throws, browserRequests sets sound = false, and the request is Lost (browser-request.ts:91-92). browserJoining returns unknown() (browser-joining.ts:115), which is the sentence on the saved page.\n\nThe server side refuses the same path: the sandbox Worker uses the same applicationGatewayRoute (apps/sandbox/worker.ts:48), and so does the scope Worker (packages/scope/src/worker.ts:850). Fixing only the client is not enough.\n\nScope of the defect: through an installed screen, every read that carries a read minimum is refused. The route allows no atLeast on the summary (parts.length 3: no search), history (cursor only), items (cursor only), application-projection (p only) or entries (no search). Joining is the first place a member meets it. packages/client/test/application-gateway.test.ts has no case with atLeast.\n\nProposal for the fix request: allow exactly one atLeast parameter, as the read-minimum encoding defines it, on the read routes that take a minimum. Add a gateway unit case per route with a named red, and a hosted NF-7 rerun with a fresh invitation. The route is shared by the client, the sandbox Worker and the scope Worker, so the landing needs a deployment of the sandbox and the room Workers. Your call on the scope: entries only, or every route that takes a minimum.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}